 {r}←Initial ps;token;cfgFilename;backup;data;msg;os;⎕TRAP
⍝ Two things are settled here before any test case runs.\\
⍝ **The access token**: an environment variable "GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN" is all that is
⍝ needed, and it takes precedence anyway, so when there is one there is nothing to say.
⍝ A token in the configuration file is a different matter: the test cases create,
⍝ overwrite and delete that very file, so a token in it does not survive the run. The
⍝ user is then told how to put it into the environment instead, and asked whether she
⍝ would rather cancel — unless we run in batch mode, when there is nobody to ask.\\
⍝ **The configuration file**: it is copied aside, because the test cases destroy it.
⍝ `Cleanup` puts it back. A copy that is there already was left behind by a run that
⍝ did not finish, and since the original may well be gone this interrupts rather than
⍝ guessing what to do with it.\\
⍝ Returns an empty vector, which lets `Tester2` carry on, or a message, which makes it
⍝ report that message and run no test at all.
 r←''
 cfgFilename←##.GitHub.GetConfigFilename
 backup←cfgFilename,'.saved-by-GitHub-tests'
 os←⎕C ##.GitHub.APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬

⍝ --- Will there be an access token?
 :If 'win'≡os
     token←2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment' 'GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN'
 :Else
     token←(⊃⎕SH'echo $GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN')~'"'
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢token                                       ⍝ Nothing in the environment, so look
     :If ##.GitHub.FilesAndDirs.IsFile cfgFilename  ⍝ into the configuration file
         data←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊢⊃⎕NGET cfgFilename
         :If 0<data.⎕NC'access_token'
             token←data.access_token
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
     :If 0<≢token                                   ⍝ In the file but not in the environment
     :AndIf 0=ps.batchFlag                          ⍝ ...and somebody is there to answer
         msg←⊂'There is an access token in the configuration file but not in the environment.'
         msg,←⊂'The test cases create, overwrite and delete that very file, so the token will'
         msg,←⊂'not survive this run: the tests will talk to GitHub unauthenticated.'
         msg,←⊂''
         msg,←⊂'Should you hit GitHub''s rate limit, cancel, make sure Cleanup ran, open a shell,'
         msg,←⊂'put the token into the environment and start Dyalog from that very shell:'
         msg,←⊂''
         :If 'win'≡os
             msg,←⊂'   set GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN=<your token>'
             msg,←⊂'   dyalog'
             msg,←⊂''
             msg,←⊂'   (in PowerShell:  $env:GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN=''<your token>'' )'
         :Else
             msg,←⊂'   export GITHUB_ACCESS_TOKEN=<your token>'
             msg,←⊂'   dyalog'
         :EndIf
         msg,←⊂''
         msg,←⊂'Would you like to cancel the tests?'
         :If 0 CommTools.YesOrNo msg                ⍝ "No" is the default
             r←'Cancelled by user'
             :Return                                ⍝ Before anything is copied anywhere
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf

⍝ --- Save the configuration file, because the test cases destroy it
 :If ##.GitHub.FilesAndDirs.IsFile backup
     msg←⊂'*** A copy of the configuration file is already there:'
     msg,←⊂'***    ',backup
     msg,←⊂'*** It was left behind by a test run that did not finish, and the original may'
     msg,←⊂'*** well have been deleted by that very run. Nothing is done automatically here.'
     msg,←⊂'***'
     msg,←⊂'*** Rename it back to'
     msg,←⊂'***    ',cfgFilename
     msg,←⊂'*** (or delete it, if you are sure it is of no use), then run the tests again.'
     ⎕←↑msg
     ⎕TRAP←0 'S'                                    ⍝ So that this really does stop
     ∘∘∘
 :ElseIf ##.GitHub.FilesAndDirs.IsFile cfgFilename
     backup ⎕NCOPY cfgFilename                      ⍝ `Cleanup` moves it back
 :EndIf
⍝Done
